{number: 78}
{title: Faith of Our Fathers}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Faith of our fathers! [G7] living [C] still,
In spite of dungeon, [F] fire, and [C] sword:
O how our hearts beat [G7] high with [C] joy
Whene’er we hear that [G7] glorious [C] word!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F] Faith of our [C] fathers, [G7] holy [C] faith!
We [F] will be [C] true to [G7] thee till [C] death.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Faith of our fathers! [G7] we will [C] strive
To win all nations [F] unto [C] thee,
And thro' the truth that [G7] comes from [C] God,
Mankind shall then be [G7] truly [C] free.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Faith of our fathers! [G7] we will [C] love
Both friend and foe in [F] all our [C] strife:
And preach thee too as [G7] love knows [C] how,
By kindly words and [G7] virtuous [C] life.
{end_of_verse}
